    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19968": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Recruitment",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Associate Director of Recruitment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Associate Director of Recruitment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please supply contact information for three professional references that can supply a letter of reference for you. Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $50,000 - $56,000 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1412026 Working Title Associate Director of Recruitment Department Org 131000 - Admissions & Enrollment Support Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary This position directly reports to the Director of Admissions and Enrollment Services and serves as a key member of the admissions leadership team. This position assists with all aspects of the undergraduate recruitment process, including recruitment strategies and implementation of on and off-campus programming and initiatives within individual territories. This position supervises all undergraduate recruitment personnel within the Admissions Department, including admission counselors and assistant directors. Job Duties and Responsibilities -Supervises all recruitment personnel -Develops and implements policies, procedures, and training for all recruitment staff -Oversees the Assistant Director of Campus Preview Days and assists with the development, execution, and reporting of all preview day events -Oversees the Assistant Director of Campus Tours and assists with the continuation of daily tour operations and the Welcome Center management -Supports the oversight of the UCA Ambassador program -Disseminates and interprets state and institutional regulations, policies, and procedures regarding admissions -Develops recruitment goals, objectives, and strategies for all designated territories -Assists in the development and expansion of the institutional CRM to ensure effective recruitment data are generated and leveraged appropriately -Assists in the development, maintenance, and execution of the departments’ communication, marketing and campaign plans for all target audiences -Contributes to annual planning and evaluation of recruitment and admission activities -Develops and monitors statistical reports to evaluate and enhance recruitment strategies within Arkansas, in contiguous states, and nationally -Presents workshops and/or training opportunities to educate individuals on admissions/recruitment initiatives -Presents to various constituencies to promote the University -Travels on behalf of the University for recruitment and other related activities -Performs other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities -Knowledge of supervisory practices and procedures -Knowledge of the principles and practices of organizational management -Knowledge of state and federal laws applicable to higher education operations and admissions -Knowledge of program planning, monitoring, and evaluation techniques -Ability to work independently and operate with flexibility in a fast-paced, evolving environment -Ability to plan work unit objectives and operational activities -Ability to evaluate operational effectiveness and compliance -Ability to prepare and present information to various constituents both on and off campus -Ability to develop and implement goals, objectives, guidelines, policies and procedures -Ability to communicate with diverse populations Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments and assist in resolving student concerns. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions of a public or confidential nature. -Demonstrate follow-up contacts and consultations in a timely manner. Required Education and/or Experience -A Bachelor’s Degree required -Minimum of two (2) years experience in Higher Education -Demonstrated abilities to work collaboratively with other personnel -Well-developed capabilities in strategic planning, problem-solving, attention to detail, and task completion -Excellent interpersonal communication and writing skills Preferred Education and/or Experience -Master’s Degree in Higher Education or related field -Experience working in university admissions or student services -Proven personal record of successful recruitment strategies -Knowledge of strategic student recruitment, prospect management processes, and metrical evaluations as they relate to university recruitment -Extensive knowledge in student management software, particularly Slate -Management experience with a diverse range of employees in terms of position titles and backgrounds -Experience in event planning and management University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 02/01/2027 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Physical Demands Checklist Sitting, Kneeling, Standing, Lifting/Carrying, Walking Physical Exertion Light Work - Exerting up to 20 pounds, Administrative Work - Exerting up to 10 pounds, Medium Work - Exerting 20-50 pounds Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/18/2026 Close Date 12/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please supply contact information for three professional references that can supply a letter of reference for you. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in higher education? 0-1 2-4 5 or more Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran's Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
