    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19972": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor I",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Clinical Instructor I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Instructor I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0572026 Working Title Clinical Instructor I Department Org 344000 - Nursing Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary UCA invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, on-campus Clinical Instructor I (faculty) position. Join a collaborative faculty dedicated to student success and clinical excellence in our CCNE -accredited baccalaureate program. More information about the School of Nursing and its program can be found at www.uca.edu/nursing . Job Duties and Responsibilities This non-tenure track position focuses on teaching didactic, clinical, simulation and laboratory courses. The faculty member will facilitate student learning, engage in scholarship/practice, and provide service at the institutional and professional levels. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The candidate MUST : Possess a passion for teaching. Articulate and speak authoritatively about the profession and its future direction. Demonstrate evidence of interpersonal skills, networking abilities, and intraprofessional and interprofessional collaboration. Create an environment that facilitates student learning and the achievement of desired outcomes. Strive to improve teaching on an on-going basis. Help students integrate the values and behaviors expected of nurses. Use a variety of strategies to assess and evaluate student learning. Assist with formulating program outcomes and designing curricula that reflect contemporary health care trends. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience The candidate MUST have: 1) Master’s degree in nursing. 2) Unencumbered RN license to practice in Arkansas. 3) Clinical and/or teaching experience in Nursing Informatics, Health Policy and Geriatric or Community Health Nursing. Candidates with other clinical specialties and job experience will be considered. Must have all clinical requirements mandated by the clinical agencies used for student clinical experiences. These requirements include: 1) MMR (2 vaccines or a positive titer), 2) Varicella (2 vaccines at least 28 days apart or positive titer), 3) Hepatitis B (2 part series or positive surface antibodies above 10), 4) Tdap (must be received within the last 10 years), 5) Tb (Initial testing: Interferon-gamma release assay ( IGRA ) or a tuberculin skin test ( TST ) for persons without documented prior testing, TB disease or latent TB infection ( LTBI ). Retesting: No annual retest or routine serial testing at any interval after baseline in the absence of a known exposure or ongoing transmission is required), 6) Influenza vaccine (annually); and 7) current CPR certification BLS from American Health Association. Preferred Education and/or Experience It is PREFERRED that the candidate has: 1) Educational preparation as a nurse educator or experience teaching at the baccalaureate level. 2) Experience with learning management systems and/or online teaching at the baccalaureate or higher degree. 3) Experience with simulation teaching at the baccalaureate level or higher. 4) Education or experience in the following nursing specialty areas: Nursing Informatics, Health Policy and Geriatric or Community Health Nursing. Candidates with clinical or job experience(s) in other nursing areas will be considered. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Licensed as an RN in Arkansas University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 01/01/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document License or Certification Veteran's Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19964": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0542026 Working Title Assistant Professor Department Org 357000 - Sociology, Criminology, and Anthropology Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Department of Sociology, Criminology, & Anthropology at the University of Central Arkansas is accepting applications for an Assistant Professor position in Criminology. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. Job Duties and Responsibilities This position is needed to teach undergraduate courses ranging from introductory criminal justice to junior/senior level electives in criminology or criminal justice. The course load for this position is four course sections per semester taught in-person, face-to-face, in a traditional classroom setting. The successful candidate should also be prepared to teach select sections in online, hybrid, or blended modes if needed. Other responsibilities include faculty meeting participation, compliance with all employee workplace training/monitoring requirements, a modest level of research production, and university/professional service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Candidates must possess deep general knowledge of, and teaching experience in, the science of criminology and/or criminal justice in the United States. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in criminology, criminal justice, or a related field with a demonstrated emphasis on research related to criminological or criminal justice topics. A commitment to excellent undergraduate teaching is paramount for success in this position and candidates must demonstrate the ability to design and deliver high-quality undergraduate courses. Additional preference will be given to candidates with research specialties that extend beyond the scholarly agendas of our current faculty. Scholars with research agendas related to crime prevention, criminal courts, criminal evidence, criminalistics, criminal law, emergency management, or victimology are especially encouraged to apply. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience A Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a related field is the minimum education required for this position. Preferred Education and/or Experience License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/17/2026 Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
