      "title": "Head Women's Volleyball Coach",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Head Women&#39;s Volleyball Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Head Women's Volleyball Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $75,000 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1422026 Working Title Head Women's Volleyball Coach Department Org 152700 - Women's Volleyball Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Head Women’s Volleyball Coach reports to the Director of Athletics and serves as a member of the department staff that is committed to excellence and advancing the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics through its strategic plan and vision. Job Duties and Responsibilities Providing direction and leadership for the Volleyball program and staff, coordinating the day-to-day operations of the program to include, but not limited to, recruiting and roster management, practicing, scheduling, planning and preparation for competition. Coordinating the logistics for all team travel to competitions including transportation, lodging, and meals. Coordinating the procurement of all team-related gear, equipment, supplies and services. Maintaining care of appropriate equipment and Central Arkansas Volleyball facilities. Monitoring the program budget to ensure fiscal responsibility and sound budgetary processes and procedures. Ensuring compliance with NCAA Division I, United Athletic Conference, and University rules and regulations. Working collaboratively with Athletic Academic Resource Center staff to monitor academic progress and student-athlete success. Serving as liaison to and work in a highly collaborative fashion with alumni and friends of the program. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong personal, writing, verbal and interpersonal communication, computer, and emotional skills. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Preferred Education and/or Experience Preferred qualifications include Bachelor’s degree, collegiate volleyball playing experience and/or collegiate coaching experience and/or professional playing experience. Knowledge of and commitment to NCAA rules with experience in collegiate coaching or experience in sport related area. Nights, weekends, and ability to travel are essential. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 12/16/2026 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Physical Demands Checklist Physical Exertion Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or