    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19990": {
      "title": "Assistant (or Assoc) Professor (Fa27)",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant (or Assoc) Professor (Fa27) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant (or Assoc) Professor (Fa27) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, (4) a teaching interest form (completed and uploaded to “other document”) available at https://uca.edu/accounting/teaching-interest-form/,and (5) if available, evidence of teaching effectiveness. Additionally, please provide contact information for three references. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0562026 Working Title Assistant (or Assoc) Professor (Fa27) Department Org 312000 - Accounting Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Assistant Professor is responsible for teaching, research, and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities An Assistant/Associate Professor at the University of Central Arkansas is expected to teach classes at the undergraduate and graduate level. The faculty member will be expected to teach a variety of accounting courses, as well as develop and maintain an active program of research leading to peer reviewed publications. In addition, providing service at a variety of levels is expected (service levels may include department, college, university, profession, academic community, and/or local community). Candidates should be willing to teach in both face to face and distance education formats. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Applicants should possess a command of the discipline, the ability to deliver effective instruction and assess student performance, and the capability of engaging in successful individual and collaborative research and scholarship. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Minimum educational requirements include either (i) an earned doctorate in Accounting with significant hours of accounting coursework prior to doctorate, (ii) a Juris Doctorate with an LLM in taxation for applicants with a desire to teach tax, or (iii) an earned doctorate in business accompanied by significant accounting experience and prior degrees in accounting. (Candidates nearing completion of an earned doctorate will also be considered for an Assistant Professor position. Candidates with a JD and no LLM , wishing to teach tax, will be considered and, if hired, expected to earn an LLM before midtenure review.) Applicants at the Associate Professor rank must also have a professional certification and an established record of research and quality teaching. Preferred Education and/or Experience Significant professional experience is desirable as well as teaching experience in either traditional or non-traditional settings. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) A CPA certification or a license to practice law is preferred. Other accounting certifications are also a plus. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, (4) a teaching interest form (completed and uploaded to “other document”) available at https://uca.edu/accounting/teaching-interest-form/,and (5) if available, evidence of teaching effectiveness. Additionally, please provide contact information for three references. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Will you include with your application materials the teaching interest form to indicate your preference and/or willingness to teach a variety of courses. The form can be found at https://uca.edu/accounting/teaching-interest-form/. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Transcripts Veteran's Documents Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19993": {
      "title": "Visiting Lecturer of Management (Business Communication)",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Visiting Lecturer of Management (Business Communication) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Lecturer of Management (Business Communication) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, and (3) a statement of teaching philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three professional references. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0662026 Working Title Visiting Lecturer of Management (Business Communication) Department Org 314000 - Marketing and Management Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas visiting faculty is responsible for teaching, professional engagement, and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is non-tenure track and a one year appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities Candidates should be able to teach courses in business communication and remain active in business practice relevant to their discipline through professional engagement activities. Responsibilities include: Provide quality teaching in the area of business communication and related areas of expertise in face-to-face and online formats Teaching load is twelve hours per term for both fall and spring semesters Sustain currency and relevance through continued engagement involving business practices through professional engagement activities as defined in our AACSB accreditation documents. Provide service to the department, college, and academic community that is commensurate with the position and experience and aligned with expertise. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Applicants should possess a command of the discipline, the ability to deliver effective instruction and assess student performance in both face-to-face and online formats, and the capability of engaging in successful individual and collaborative professional engagement activities relevant to their discipline that fits with AACSB standards. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Candidates should hold an MBA or a master’s degree in Communication, Business Communication, or a master’s degree in a closely related field. A DBA or PhD in Management or Communication would alternatively meet the degree requirement. Preferred Education and/or Experience Professional experience is desirable, as well as teaching experience in either traditional or non-traditional settings. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, and (3) a statement of teaching philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three professional references. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Veteran's Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
