    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20010": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Legacy Planning",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Senior Director of Legacy Planning Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Director of Legacy Planning Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must apply online through https://jobs.uca.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Please include the following documents with your application: Resume Cover Letter The University of Central Arkansas is committed to enhancing the diversity of its faculty and staff and encourages applications from women, minorities, members of the LBGT community, people with disabilities and veterans. The University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $85,000 - $95,000 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1452026 Working Title Senior Director of Legacy Planning Department Org 200150-Office of Legacy Planning Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas is seeking a dynamic, relationship-driven fundraising professional to serve as its Senior Director of Legacy Planning. Reporting to the Associate Vice President of Campaign and Development, this position will direct the Office of Legacy Planning and drive the University’s comprehensive gift planning strategy during a pivotal moment of institutional momentum. Aligned with UCA 2035—the University’s new ten-year strategic plan—this role will play a central part in securing deferred and blended gifts that fund UCA’s “margin of excellence” and long-term campaign priorities. Guided by our mission to provide a lifetime impact for students by securing private support and enriching the University brand, UCA Advancement has surpassed $10 million in annual giving for nine consecutive years—closing FY26 with $14.4 million raised, a record $6.1 million in planned gifts, and 144 Doyne Legacy Society households. Striving to be a compelling force in the University’s continuous pursuit of academic excellence, we build lifelong relationships with alumni, families, and friends to foster a lasting culture of engagement and philanthropy. Advancement professionals at UCA are relationship-focused, alumni- and donor-centric, collaborative, ethical, and results-oriented—committed to excellence and consistently challenging ourselves and each other to achieve higher levels of impact. Job Duties and Responsibilities Essential Functions Fundraising, Marketing & External Outreach Actively identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit and steward donors capable of making a deferred gift to the University. Manage a portfolio of prospects and advisors and generate 10-15 meaningful contacts per month leading to the growth in the number of completed planned, major, and blended gift solicitations. Local, regional, and limited national travel are required. Provide personalized illustrations of planned gifts for prospects as needed. Build and nurture strong relationships with financial, legal and tax advisors. Work with the Senior Director of Advancement Communications to create comprehensive planned giving marketing strategies and proposals and to refine program materials including letters, newsletters, brochures, and stories for UCA publications. Internal Collaboration Serve as a member of the development team and as a resource to Directors of Development on issues related to planned giving. Partner with Directors of Development in identifying planned giving prospects within their portfolios and collaborate with them on solicitation strategies. Provide timely stewardship of assigned donors, prospects, and Doyne Legacy Society members. In coordination with the Director of Donor Relations & Events, plan stewardship events and recognition activities to strategically grow Doyne Legacy Society membership. Program Tools & Estate Administration Manage the Crescendo and FreeWill planned giving tools and vendor relationships. Monitor engagement and responses from online planned giving activity and research each to identify new prospects. Track mature estate expectancies to ensure the preservation and timely distribution of all estate gifts to the University of Central Arkansas Foundation. Communicate closely with advancement services staff regarding information pertaining to major and planned gift prospects, including contact reports, proposal generation, gift acknowledgement and other data important for the maintenance of donor/prospect records. Keep up to date and be proficient with state and federal regulations for planned giving. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of planned and life income gift opportunities, gift and estate tax regulations and major gift fundraising Strong operational and organizational skills Demonstrated ability to form and fully leverage cross-functional teams of colleagues, volunteers, and academic/University leaders toward closure of transformational gifts Strong communication skills, including the ability to speak and write effectively and persuasively; draft compelling proposals and letters Exceptional professional interpersonal skills, including ability to accept input as well as supervisory guidance Ability to work independently and as a part of a team Ability to manage time well, particularly while managing competing priorities Ability to manage budgets and allocate resources effectively and responsibly Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor’s degree, preferably in finance, communications, business administration or related field. Five or more years of successful fundraising experience may substitute for the bachelor’s degree requirement. Five or more years of successful fundraising experience or equivalent experience in a related field. Understanding of estate planning and other deferred giving vehicles. Valid driver’s license Preferred Education and/or Experience Higher education fundraising experience Certified Fund Raising Executive ( CFRE ) Planned giving/financial planner certifications Knowledge of alumni and development data systems (Raiser’s Edge NXT and Gravyty Raise preferred) Master’s degree University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 02/16/2027 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Physical Demands Checklist Sitting Physical Exertion Administrative Work - Exerting up to 10 pounds, Primarily indoor work Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates must apply online through https://jobs.uca.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Please include the following documents with your application: Resume Cover Letter The University of Central Arkansas is committed to enhancing the diversity of its faculty and staff and encourages applications from women, minorities, members of the LBGT community, people with disabilities and veterans. The University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Portfolio / Supplemental Materials License or Certification Leadership Statement Other Transcripts Veteran's Documents Additional Documents Class Schedule University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
