    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20017": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of English Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of English Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates should apply at http://jobs.uca.edu. Completed applications must include: ● a letter of application outlining one’s interest in and qualifications for the position. ● a CV. ● contact information for three professional references. ● a professional writing sample of 15-20 pages. ● a teaching portfolio that consists of: (1) a teaching philosophy; (2) a sample syllabus for a survey of American literature; and (3) a sample syllabus for an advanced undergraduate course American literature. For consideration, applications must be received no later than January 15, 2027. Address queries to Dr. Glenn Jellenik, SLL Director and professor of English, atgjellenik@uca.edu; or Dr. Lori Leavell, professor of English and chair of the searchcommittee, at lleavell@uca.edu. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0602026 Working Title Assistant Professor of English Department Org 354000 School of Language and Literature Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Assistant Professor is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The School of Language and Literature ( SLL ) at the University of Central Arkansas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English to start in August 2027. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment. SLL at UCA houses degree programs in Chinese, English, French, Japanese, linguistics, Spanish, and TESOL . SLL is home to more than 250 majors or minors. The English Program offers the BA in English, the BA in English with teaching licensure, and the MA in English. Program faculty are highly engaged in scholarly production and learner-centered pedagogies. UCA English currently serves more than 100 undergraduate majors and 45 minors. Additionally, faculty have opportunities to teach in support of several interdisciplinary minors, UCA’s residential-college programs, and the honors college. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities involve lower- and upper-division undergraduate courses, including general education courses, and/or graduate seminars in relevant literary traditions. Mentoring of students is expected at both the graduate and undergraduate level. Service includes committee-work for the School, College, and University. The position includes support for advancing one’s scholarship and faculty mentorship. The teaching load for the position is 4/4, but may be distributed as 50-75% classroom instruction, 25-50% supervision of Residencies in field placement (Internships) for our English Education program, depending on the candidate’s expertise. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Required qualifications for this position include: ● completion of the Ph.D. in English no later than August 1, 2027. ● at least one year of successful teaching experience at the university level. ● specialization in American literature, as demonstrated by completed graduate coursework, comprehensive-examination emphases, dissertation subject matter, juried presentations, and/or peer-reviewed publication. Preferred Education and/or Experience Ideal candidates will be: ● possessed of significant, successful teaching experience in literature. ● pursuing a scholarly agenda focused on non-dramatic American literature. ● adept in teaching general-education courses on poetry and film and literature. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Interested candidates should apply at http://jobs.uca.edu. Completed applications must include: ● a letter of application outlining one’s interest in and qualifications for the position. ● a CV. ● contact information for three professional references. ● a professional writing sample of 15-20 pages. ● a teaching portfolio that consists of: (1) a teaching philosophy; (2) a sample syllabus for a survey of American literature; and (3) a sample syllabus for an advanced undergraduate course American literature. For consideration, applications must be received no later than January 15, 2027. Address queries to Dr. Glenn Jellenik, SLL Director and professor of English, atgjellenik@uca.edu; or Dr. Lori Leavell, professor of English and chair of the searchcommittee, at lleavell@uca.edu. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Writing Sample Portfolio / Supplemental Materials Additional Documents Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20012": {
      "title": "Lecturer I",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Lecturer I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0612026 Working Title Lecturer I Department Org 357000 - Sociology, Criminology, and Anthropology Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Department of Sociology, Criminology, & Anthropology at the University of Central Arkansas is accepting applications for a full-time position as a Lecturer in Criminology. We seek candidates with a broad-general understanding of criminal justice and strong teaching skills to join a convivial department of sociologists, criminologists, and anthropologists. This position is governed by state laws, federal laws, and department/institution policies. The position is non-tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities Lecturers are expected to be committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring. This position is needed to teach a range of courses that cover criminal justice principles, practices, systems, and processes with an emphasis on the United States. The course load for this position is four course sections per semester taught in-person, face-to-face, in a traditional classroom setting. The successful candidate should also be prepared, if needed, to teach select sections in online, hybrid, or blended modes. Other responsibilities include faculty meeting participation, supporting criminology-related student organizations, and compliance with all employee workplace training/monitoring requirements. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Candidates must possess broad-based general knowledge of criminology and criminal justice systems in the United States. Candidates must have an established record of teaching experience in criminology/criminal justice courses. For this position, a commitment to excellent undergraduate teaching is paramount. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience A J.D. or a master’s degree in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or related fields is the minimum education required for this position. Preferred Education and/or Experience Candidates who have recent practical experience working in some element of the criminal justice system are preferred. Additional preference will be given to candidates with experience designing and delivering undergraduate courses in at least one of the following areas: introductory criminal justice, criminal prosecution, criminal evidence, criminal victimization, crime prevention, or criminal courts. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20014": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management (Strategy), tenure-track",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Management (Strategy), tenure-track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Management (Strategy), tenure-track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (4) a research philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three letters of reference. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0642026 Working Title Assistant Professor of Management (Strategy), tenure-track Department Org 314000 - Marketing and Management Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Assistant Professor is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities Candidates for the position of Assistant Professor of Management (Strategy), tenure-track should be able to teach courses in strategy and conduct relevant research. A secondary emphasis in entrepreneurship is desirable. Strong candidates will be willing and able to teach a suitable range of classes, maintain a program of research appropriate for college AACSB standards, and provide appropriate service. Responsibilities include: Provide quality teaching in the area of strategic management and related areas of expertise in face-to-face and online formats Teaching load is twelve hours per term with three hours of research release time (3/3 teaching load for the tenure-track role) for both fall and spring semesters The option to teach in the summer is often available, pursuant to student demand Produce quality research (as applicable) leading to published scholarly contributions in accordance with departmental and college expectations related to AACSB accreditation Provide service to the department, college, and academic community that is commensurate with rank and experience and aligned with expertise Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Applicants should possess a command of the discipline, the ability to deliver effective instruction and assess student performance in both face-to-face and online formats, and the capability of engaging in successful individual and collaborative research and scholarship relevant to their discipline that fits with AACSB standards. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Candidates should hold a DBA or Ph.D. in Management, Strategy, or Business Administration ( ABD considered) or a closely related field. Preferred Education and/or Experience Professional experience is desirable, as well as teaching experience in either traditional or non-traditional settings. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (4) a research philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three letters of reference. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
