    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20021": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Choral Music Education",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor-Choral Music Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor-Choral Music Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide one teaching segment video and one rehearsal segment video in the form of links underneath the portfolio portion of the application. Also provide three professional contacts that can serve as a professional reference. To receive full consideration please submit your application before January 18, 2026. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0582026 Working Title Assistant Professor-Choral Music Education Department Org 335000 - Music Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position of Choral Music Education in the School of Music. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teaching duties include conducting one choral ensemble and supervising professional internships (residencies) for choral music education majors. Depending on qualifications, other teaching duties may include secondary choral methods, advanced choral conducting, vocal methods for instrumentalists, and courses in the MME Program. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Required knowledge and skills include: programming, recruiting, and conducting an undergraduate choral ensemble; placement and supervision of professional internships (residencies); knowledge of vocal pedagogy, choral pedagogy, rehearsal technique, voice classification, IPA , literature selection, score study, sight-singing, and the AR and national Frameworks and Standards for Music Education. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience PhD in Music Education, a DMA in Choral Conducting, or equivalent. Experience teaching and conducting 7-12 grade students in choral music is required. Preferred Education and/or Experience Successful teaching in a public school setting for 3-5 years. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide one teaching segment video and one rehearsal segment video in the form of links underneath the portfolio portion of the application. Also provide three professional contacts that can serve as a professional reference. To receive full consideration please submit your application before January 18, 2026. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Additional Documents Optional Documents Resume University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/20013": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing, tenure-track",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Marketing, tenure-track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Marketing, tenure-track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (4) a research philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three letters of reference. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0632026 Working Title Assistant Professor of Marketing, tenure-track Department Org 314000 - Marketing and Management Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Assistant Professor is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities Candidates for the position, Assistant Professor of Marketing, tenure-track should be able to teach courses in marketing and conduct relevant research. An ability to teach Marketing Research is preferred. Strong candidates will be willing and able to teach a suitable range of classes, maintain a program of research appropriate for college AACSB standards, and provide appropriate service. Responsibilities include: Provide quality teaching in the area of Marketing, Marketing Research, and related areas of expertise in face-to-face and online formats Teaching load is twelve hours per term with three hours of research release time (3/3 teaching load for this tenure-track role) for both fall and spring semesters The option to teach in the summer is often available, pursuant to student demand Produce quality research (as applicable) leading to published scholarly contributions in accordance with departmental and college expectations related to AACSB accreditation Provide service to the department, college, and academic community that is commensurate with rank and experience and aligned with expertise Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Applicants should possess a command of the discipline, the ability to deliver effective instruction and assess student performance in both face-to-face and online formats, and the capability of engaging in successful individual and collaborative research and scholarship relevant to their discipline that fits with AACSB standards. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Candidates should hold a DBA or Ph.D. in Marketing ( ABD considered) or a closely related field. Preferred Education and/or Experience Professional experience is desirable, as well as teaching experience in either traditional or non-traditional settings. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants should include the following documents: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of application, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (4) a research philosophy. Additionally, please provide contact information for three letters of reference. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
